{"id":"datemultical","name":"datemultical","aliases":[],"caption":"Named dates, calendar conversion, and date formatting for LaTeX","authors":[{"id":"amikhteh","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Amer Amikhteh","year":"2026"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"0.2.0","date":"2026-10-18"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      This package provides a unified interface for defining,\n      converting, and formatting named dates in multiple calendar\n      systems in LaTeX.\n      It provides a built-in TeX backend supporting the Gregorian,\n      Solar Hijri, and Lunar Hijri calendars under supported TeX engines,\n      and an extended LuaLaTeX backend that additionally interfaces\n      with <ref refid=\"lua-calendrica\">lua-calendrica<\u002fref> to support\n      a wide range of historical, astronomical, and traditional calendar\n      systems.\n      Dates can be stored under user-defined names, converted\n      between supported calendars, and retrieved through a common\n      field-based interface.\n      The package provides predefined date styles and customizable\n      formatting patterns, including calendar-specific month and\n      weekday names, week information, and leap-year, leap-month,\n      and leap-day fields.\n      Persian localization and high-level Persian date and\n      weekday wrappers are also provided.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/datemultical/doc/datemultical.pdf"},{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/datemultical/README.md"}],"bugs":"https://github.com/gambi-shah/datemultical/issues","repository":"https://github.com/gambi-shah/datemultical","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/datemultical","file":true},"miktex":"datemultical","texlive":"datemultical","topics":["use-luatex","persian","date-time","calendar"]}